  "a_point": "When assessing the insured's residual capacity for work based on expert evidence, the Federal Supreme Court confirms that the cantonal court may rely on an expert report from another insurance branch (here, the accident insurer's judicial expert) without ordering a new examination, provided the expert's findings are complete, consistent, and not contradicted by other medical evidence; it also holds that the existence of a psychiatric diagnosis does not automatically entitle the insured to a disability pension if the treating psychiatrist does not certify any work‑related incapacity and the court can refuse a structured proof procedure when no medically attested psychiatric incapacity exists.",
